  DailyReading(170, "The Right Word at the Right Time", "Proverbs 25:11", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in settings of silver."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The proverb compares a fitting word to beautiful gold fruit in a silver setting. The image values words well placed within their circumstances. Wisdom asks what the listener needs now, not merely whether the speaker has something accurate or clever to say.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Before raising a concern, ask whether the other person has space to hear it. A planned conversation may serve the issue better than an impulsive remark.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
