  ]),
  DailyReading(172, "Grow Through Thoughtful Challenge", "Proverbs 27:17", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Iron sharpens iron; so a man sharpens his friend’s countenance."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The proverb compares people shaping one another to iron sharpening iron. The image recognizes mutual influence. It supports growth through real engagement, while respectful challenge remains different from humiliation, relentless criticism, or the claim that one person should dominate another's judgment and choices.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Discuss an idea with someone who can question it kindly. A good conversation can make the idea more useful without turning the difference into a contest.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can welcome relationships that help you think more clearly and live more responsibly, remembering that encouragement sometimes includes a respectful challenge rather than immediate agreement with your view.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
