    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "If you are replaying an exchange, decide whether it needs action, a boundary, or release. Another round of private argument may not provide what you need.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can notice anger without giving it a permanent home in your thoughts, allowing yourself time to understand the hurt and choose a response that serves what is right.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
