        "Let one task wait briefly while you pray or read. You can return to your responsibilities with less resentment when attention and receiving also have room.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can give Jesus your attention without earning that moment through finished chores. Mary chose to listen while the household still held plenty of activity.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
        "Caring God, help me notice my need for rest. Give me freedom to set down what cannot be finished today, courage to ask for help, and wisdom to care for the body and life entrusted to me. Let rest become an expression of trust. Amen.\n\nCarry this with you: You can give Jesus your attention without earning that moment through finished chores. Mary chose to listen while the household still held plenty of activity."),
