    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "If you have been avoiding prayer, begin with one true sentence. You can acknowledge what went wrong and take a practical step toward repairing its effects.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can turn back toward God without composing a perfect explanation first. In Jesus' story, the father moves toward his returning son with visible compassion.\n\nLet this be a steady reminder rather than another demand to perform well. Remembering God's care can make space for a more patient response to yourself and to others. Today's limits are real, and there can still be something faithful and good within them."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
