  DailyReading(255, "Giving With Strong and Gentle Hands", "Acts 20:35", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "In all things I gave you an example, that so laboring you ought to help the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, that he himself said, ‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’ ”"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Paul's example involves labor that serves more than his own comfort. Remembering Jesus' words, he directs attention toward the good of giving. This does not erase receiving; a healthy community makes room for people to offer and accept help.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Consider where your present capacity could make a difference today. You can offer one useful thing without assuming you must personally answer every need you see.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
