  DailyReading(256, "Peace Before Your Performance", "Romans 5:1", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Being therefore justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ;"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Justification describes being put right with God through Christ. The peace Paul names is therefore more than a passing calm feeling. You can have difficult emotions without concluding that your relationship with God must be broken beyond repair.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "If you feel anxious during prayer today, you do not need to measure acceptance by that feeling. Turn toward Jesus and speak with simple honesty.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can approach God through Jesus rather than through a daily score of spiritual success. Paul grounds peace with God in faith, not flawless personal performance.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
