  DailyReading(259, "Give Your Mind a Better Pattern", "Romans 12:2", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Don’t be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind, so that you may prove what is the good, well-pleasing, and perfect will of God."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Transformation includes attention to how you interpret life, not only outward behavior. Repeated messages about worth, success, and fear can become familiar without becoming true. Renewing your mind invites you to test those messages against the character and teaching of God.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Choose one repeated thought to examine today. You can ask whether it leads toward truth and love, then practice a more faithful way to describe the situation.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can question the patterns that have been shaping your thoughts. Paul describes renewal of the mind as part of learning to recognize God's good way.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
        "Wise and loving God, guide my attention to what is true and good. Help me listen before deciding, consider those affected by my choices, and welcome correction without defensiveness. Give me patience to seek understanding and courage to act responsibly. Amen.\n\nCarry this with you: You can question the patterns that have been shaping your thoughts. Paul describes renewal of the mind as part of learning to recognize God's good way."),
  ]),
  DailyReading(260, "Your Part in Making Peace", "Romans 12:18", [
