    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "You can show up for one worthwhile task without pretending to be invulnerable. Honest limits and real contribution can occupy the same ordinary day together.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can carry something valuable while remaining visibly human. Paul describes God's treasure within fragile vessels, making weakness compatible with a meaningful life of faith.\n\nLet this be a steady reminder rather than another demand to perform well. Remembering God's care can make space for a more patient response to yourself and to others. Today's limits are real, and there can still be something faithful and good within them."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
