        "Being a new creation points to what God makes possible in Christ. It does not require instant perfection or erased memories. You can live from a new center while taking time to heal, unlearn patterns, and repair what remains within reach.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Choose one action that agrees with the life you are growing into today. A small honest change can matter even when old feelings still return.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
