    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Notice one good thing carefully today instead of scrolling past it. You can let a truthful, lovely detail sit beside the difficult realities you also need to face.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can choose where your attention rests without denying what is painful. Paul invites thought toward what is true, honorable, just, pure, lovely, and worthy of praise.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
