  DailyReading(300, "Notice Love Getting Stronger", "2 Thessalonians 1:3", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "We are bound to always give thanks to God for you, brothers, even as it is appropriate, because your faith grows exceedingly, and the love of each and every one of you toward one another abounds,"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The believers faced pressure, yet their shared care was increasing. Paul names that growth aloud. You can learn to look for signs of grace within a community: generosity, patience, honest repair, and the willingness to carry one another's burdens.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Think of one relationship that has grown more caring over time. You can thank God for that change and tell someone what you have noticed today.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can notice growth that appears in the way people love one another. Paul gives thanks for expanding faith and love, rather than only for outward success.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
