  DailyReading(301, "Comfort Rooted in Grace", "2 Thessalonians 2:16", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Now our Lord Jesus Christ himself, and God our Father, who loved us and gave us eternal comfort and good hope through grace,"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "This blessing points toward God and Jesus as the source of comfort. Grace means the gift is not a reward for managing hardship impressively. You can ask for encouragement in the middle of weakness, without first turning your life into evidence of success.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Let one trustworthy promise from Scripture accompany a hard task today. You can receive comfort while still asking for the practical support the situation calls for.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can seek comfort from a love that does not depend on earning it. Paul describes lasting encouragement and good hope as gifts received through grace.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
