  DailyReading(302, "Keep the Good Sustainable", "2 Thessalonians 3:13", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "But you, brothers, don’t be weary in doing what is right."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The instruction arrives within teaching about responsible shared life. It is not a demand to carry unlimited work or protect unhealthy arrangements. Perseverance can include adjusting how you serve so that your care remains honest, wise, and sustainable over time.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Choose one good action to continue today and one unnecessary pressure to release. That combination can help you keep going without letting resentment take over your effort.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can continue doing what is right without pretending you never get tired. Paul's encouragement recognizes the need to persevere when good work begins to feel wearying.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
