  DailyReading(303, "Mercy Starts With the Truth", "1 Timothy 1:15", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "The saying is faithful and worthy of all acceptance, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am chief."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Paul's testimony does not make his past a performance of shame. It makes the reach of grace visible. You do not need to minimize your wrong choices, but neither must you treat them as stronger than the invitation to turn toward Christ.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Bring one specific failure into prayer today. You can seek forgiveness and begin repairing its effects without deciding that your whole story is beyond good.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
