  DailyReading(306, "Enough Without the Endless Chase", "1 Timothy 6:6", [
    ReadingCard("scripture", "But godliness with contentment is great gain."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Contentment does not mean ignoring hunger, debt, or unfairness. It challenges the belief that your worth and security will finally arrive with the next acquisition. You can address real needs while recognizing gifts that the endless chase teaches you to overlook.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Before one optional purchase or comparison today, pause. Ask whether you need the thing itself or the feeling you hope it will provide, then choose thoughtfully.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
