    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Ask one question of today's passage: what might it teach or change in me? You can take a clear response seriously without pretending that every verse is simple.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can receive Scripture as more than a source of comforting phrases. Paul describes its usefulness for teaching, correction, and learning a life shaped by what is right.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
