  DailyReading(319, "An Anchor Beneath Changing Feelings", "Hebrews 6:19", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "This hope we have as an anchor of the soul, a hope both sure and steadfast and entering into that which is within the veil,"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "An anchor matters because the water is not always still. The passage connects security with God's trustworthy promise and Jesus' presence before him. Your ability to feel settled every moment is not what gives that hope its strength or lasting direction.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Recall one trustworthy promise while feelings shift today. You can let it steady a small decision without demanding that every anxious sensation disappear immediately from your body.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can have a steady place for hope while your emotions move around. Hebrews compares hope in God's promise to an anchor holding the soul.\n\nLet this be a steady reminder rather than another demand to perform well. Remembering God's care can make space for a more patient response to yourself and to others. Today's limits are real, and there can still be something faithful and good within them."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
