  DailyReading(323, "Lay Down a Weight for the Road", "Hebrews 12:1", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Therefore let’s also, seeing we are surrounded by so great a cloud of witnesses, lay aside every weight and the sin which so easily entangles us, and let’s run with perseverance the race that is set before us,"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The race is yours to run, supported by the witness of those who trusted God before you. Some burdens are unavoidable, but others hinder your response. Honest attention can help you distinguish necessary responsibility from habits, comparisons, or sins that keep catching your feet.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
