  DailyReading(324, "Learning Can Be Uncomfortable", "Hebrews 12:11", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "All chastening seems for the present to be not joyous but grievous; yet afterward it yields the peaceful fruit of righteousness to those who have been trained by it."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The passage concerns God's formation of his people, not permission for abuse or a claim that every injury is divine punishment. Healthy correction serves a good purpose. You can evaluate counsel by its truth and its movement toward a more faithful, peaceable life.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Consider one correction worth receiving today. You can take a useful lesson seriously while rejecting humiliation and seeking help where a relationship or setting is harmful.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
