  ]),
  DailyReading(352, "Love Begins Before Your Response", "1 John 4:10", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "In this is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son as the atoning sacrifice for our sins."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The verse points toward Christ's sacrifice as the expression of love already given. Your response matters, but it is a response rather than a purchase. You can approach God with gratitude and honesty instead of trying to perform your way into his concern.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Before one act of service or prayer today, remember why you are responding. Let being loved loosen the pressure to make every good action prove that you deserve care.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can stop treating God's love as something your effort must first awaken. John places the beginning of love in God's action toward us through his Son.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
