  ]),
  DailyReading(353, "Prayer That Leaves Room for God", "1 John 5:14", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "This is the boldness which we have toward him, that if we ask anything according to his will, he listens to us."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Asking according to God's will does not require you to know every hidden detail of the future. It invites alignment with his character and purposes. You can speak plainly about what you want while remaining open to wisdom beyond your preferred answer.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Make one honest request today, then ask how love and truth might shape your response. You can stay attentive without treating prayer as a guarantee of your chosen outcome.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
