  ]),
  DailyReading(354, "Love Has a Path to Walk", "2 John 1:6", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "This is love, that we should walk according to his commandments. This is the commandment, even as you heard from the beginning, that you should walk in it."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Walking involves repeated steps rather than a single display of feeling. The command to love guides how believers treat one another in truth. You can ask what faithful love requires in an ordinary situation, even when an emotional sense of devotion is quiet.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Choose one step of obedience that serves real love today. It may be telling the truth, keeping a promise, or giving a person your full and respectful attention.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
