  ]),
  DailyReading(355, "The Joy of Seeing Truth Lived", "3 John 1:4", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "I have no greater joy than this: to hear about my children walking in truth."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The joy in this verse comes from a lived direction, not merely correct statements. Someone is putting truth into practice. You can learn to notice that in others, encouraging their honest response without taking ownership of their story or comparing it with your own.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Think of someone whose faithful choices have encouraged you. Tell them specifically what you noticed, and let their growth become a reason for gratitude rather than comparison.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can find joy in another person's faithful growth without making it a reflection of your own importance. John celebrates people who are walking in truth.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
    ReadingCard("prayer",
