  ]),
  DailyReading(356, "Keep Close to the Love Given", "Jude 1:21", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Keep yourselves in God’s love, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ to eternal life."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Keeping yourself in God's love does not mean making him love you through effort. It means continuing within the relationship his mercy opens. Prayer, faithful attention, and loving action help you stay oriented toward that love while much remains unfinished around you.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Choose one practice that helps you remember your belonging today. It can be small enough to repeat, rather than another ambitious demand that adds pressure to your life.\n\nBring this truth into the next part of your routine. It might meet you while preparing a meal, waiting for a message, or finishing a demanding task. A small response made with care can matter even when no one else sees it."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can keep returning to God's love while waiting for the mercy of Jesus. Jude gives the life of faith a direction of belonging, expectation, and hope.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
