  DailyReading(358, "Your Days Within a Larger Story", "Revelation 1:8", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "“I am the Alpha and the Omega,” says the Lord God, “who is and who was and who is to come, the Almighty.”"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "Alpha and Omega are the first and last letters of the Greek alphabet. The image gives history its larger frame in God. Your changing season matters, yet it does not have to carry the weight of defining all that has been or will be.\n\nRead this passage as part of the larger biblical story. Its comfort is not a promise that life will become easy or that faithful people will avoid loss. It points toward a relationship with God that can sustain honest trust within real circumstances."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Take one concern out of the center of your whole story today. You can address it carefully while remembering a faithfulness that reaches beyond your current horizon.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can remember that your present moment is not the whole span of reality. God names himself as the One who is, was, and is to come.\n\nThis truth can travel with you beyond these few minutes. When attention scatters or the day changes unexpectedly, return to what the passage actually says. You are allowed to grow slowly, to seek wise counsel, and to hold hope without pretending to know the outcome."),
