  DailyReading(359, "Make Room for Renewed Fellowship", "Revelation 3:20", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears my voice and opens the door, then I will come in to him and will dine with him, and he with me."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The passage addresses a community that has become self-satisfied and lukewarm. Jesus' invitation makes room for honest return rather than mere appearance. You can ask where your own faith has become distant and respond without pretending the distance was never there.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Set aside a few minutes to be honestly present with Jesus today. You can begin with the simple admission that you want to make more room.\n\nYou may find that this becomes clearer through practice rather than through a sudden feeling. Let one interaction today be shaped by patience and attention. If the day is difficult, begin again gently; a hard moment does not erase the possibility of a faithful next step."),
