  DailyReading(360, "A Song With Room for Many Voices", "Revelation 5:9", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "They sang a new song, saying, “You are worthy to take the book and to open its seals, for you were killed, and bought us for God with your blood out of every tribe, language, people, and nation,"),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "The song centers the worth of Jesus and the cost of his redeeming love. Human difference is not erased into one narrow culture. You can honor the shared belonging of believers while listening carefully to experiences and traditions different from your own.\n\nNotice where the passage places its emphasis. God's character comes before the response it invites. Receiving these words is not a test of how spiritual you feel. You can approach them with questions, uncertainty, and a willingness to keep learning within the wider story of Scripture."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Let this wider picture challenge one assumption today. You can learn from a believer with a different background and welcome their voice without needing it to sound like yours.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
