  DailyReading(362, "Tell the Truth About Grace", "Revelation 12:11", [
    ReadingCard("scripture",
        "They overcame him because of the Lamb’s blood, and because of the word of their testimony. They didn’t love their life, even to death."),
    ReadingCard("meaning",
        "This is a vision of costly allegiance to Jesus, not a command to seek danger or neglect your safety. The believers' witness rests on the Lamb before it rests on their words. Your courage can grow from grace rather than a demand to appear invincible.\n\nThe setting matters: Scripture speaks into human lives, communities, questions, and struggles. Let the words keep their original meaning before making a connection to your own day. Faithfulness grows through patient attention, rather than through forcing a quick answer from a single verse."),
    ReadingCard("encouragement",
        "Name one truthful account of God's mercy in your life today. You can share it with care, without exaggeration or pressure to make your story sound dramatic.\n\nThere is room for an ordinary beginning. A sincere conversation, an offer of help, or a decision to pause before responding can express faith in everyday life. You do not need to solve the whole situation before doing the next loving and responsible thing."),
    ReadingCard("hope",
        "You can hold to the truth of what Christ has done when accusation feels powerful. Revelation connects victory with the Lamb's sacrifice and faithful testimony under pressure.\n\nYou do not have to manufacture certainty to receive encouragement. Hold this truth alongside the parts of your life that remain unfinished. Hope can share space with grief, questions, and practical action; it need not silence any of them before it becomes meaningful."),
